{"name":"Suffragette Yellow","hex":"#ecd0a1","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"suffragette","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A female supporter, often militant, of women's right to vote in the early 20th century, especially in Great Britain."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suffragette"},{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Suffragette","blocks":[{"text":"A suffragette was a member or supporter of the British Women's Social and Political Union (WSPU), an activist women's group agitating for votes for women, which in the early 20th century broke away from the much larger, peaceful and longer lasting National Union of Women's Suffrage Societies (NUWSS), whose supporters were known as suffragists. Both organisations campaigned for the right to vote in public elections in the United Kingdom. However, the Women's Social and Political Union, a women-only movement founded in 1903 by Emmeline Pankhurst, engaged in direct action and civil disobedience as a result of what they saw as slow progress towards universal suffrage. In 1906, a journalist writing in the Daily Mail coined the term suffragette for the WSPU, derived from suffragistα, reportedly to 'indicate that special revolutionary quality of impatience which marked the new variety of suffragist', although Elizabeth Crawford, a researcher and author on the women's suffrage movement, has suggested it was to 'belittle and to show that they were less than the proper kind of suffrage worker'. Whatever the truth was, the militants embraced the new name, even adopting it for use as the title of the newspaper published by the WSPU."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Annie_Kenney_and_Christabel_Pankhurst_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Annie_Kenney_and_Christabel_Pankhurst_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suffragette"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Votes_for_women_1909_card_back_design.jpg/500px-Votes_for_women_1909_card_back_design.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Votes_for_women_1909_card_back_design.jpg/1280px-Votes_for_women_1909_card_back_design.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Votes_for_women_1909_card_back_design.jpg/500px-Votes_for_women_1909_card_back_design.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"De La Rue playing cards back from 1910[7]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVotes_for_women_1909_card_back_design.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Emmeline_Pankhurst2.jpg/500px-Emmeline_Pankhurst2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Emmeline_Pankhurst2.jpg/500px-Emmeline_Pankhurst2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Emmeline Pankhurst founded the WSPU in 1903 and became the most prominent of Britain's suffragettes.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEmmeline_Pankhurst2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Mrs_Lilian_Metge.jpg/500px-Mrs_Lilian_Metge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Mrs_Lilian_Metge.jpg/1280px-Mrs_Lilian_Metge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Mrs_Lilian_Metge.jpg/500px-Mrs_Lilian_Metge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mannequin of Lilian Metge","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMrs_Lilian_Metge.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/%22The_Daily_Mirror%22_Frontpage%2C_March_21%2C_1907%2C_with_headline_%22Suffragettes_Storm_The_House%22.jpg/500px-%22The_Daily_Mirror%22_Frontpage%2C_March_21%2C_1907%2C_with_headline_%22Suffragettes_Storm_The_House%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.